{"title":"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) For which values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b9b7a46559a729577c3ca04dd2d7e66de16b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is there a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> consecutive <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a> such that the largest number in the set is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisor</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Least_common_multiple\" title=\"Least common multiple\">least common multiple</a> of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> numbers?\n</p><p>(b) For which values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b9b7a46559a729577c3ca04dd2d7e66de16b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is there exactly one set having the stated property?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/4/844cad1d71d680b05f2840ff51d59fd2df097745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\prod p_i^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"83\" height=\"31\" /> be the greatest element of the set, written in its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_factorization\" title=\"Prime factorization\">prime factorization</a>.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> divides the least common multiple of the other elements of the set if and only if the set has <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cardinality\" title=\"Cardinality\">cardinality</a> at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6f407120c87e320e4288f399766dfebb0acc75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max \\{ p_i^{e_i} \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />, since for any of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4101abf229ca5198f3e9fb26f0931354f0ea5b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_i^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, we must go down at least to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21a91dc3adad3ee2ed56a98cdff518c902b50e44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-p_i^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> to obtain another <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiple\" title=\"Multiple\">multiple</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4101abf229ca5198f3e9fb26f0931354f0ea5b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_i^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />.  In particular, there is no set of cardinality 3 satisfying our conditions, because each number greater than or equal to 3 must be divisible by a number that is greater than two and is a power of a prime.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd69ad8f022ee1b5894dee7cafb68305b47c9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, we may let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69aee6c6ce1c647a670a86a715dc72409fe14007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\mbox{lcm} (n-1, n-2) = (n-1)(n-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />, since all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4101abf229ca5198f3e9fb26f0931354f0ea5b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_i^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> must clearly be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and this product must also be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is at least 4.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e460097db4d7cd8b841ec11a5c9de2fd8ecde92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, we may also let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f363be300ce589766d696b99c6359360422144d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\mbox{lcm} (n-2, n-3) = (n-2)(n-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />, for the same reasons.  However, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, this does not work, and indeed no set works other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76fcbd662ca0fab5e1c0ead9f166d3617e18bc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 3,4,5,6 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />.  To prove this, we simply note that for any integer not equal to 6 and greater than 4 must have some power-of-a-prime factor greater than 3.\n</p><p>Q.E.D.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternate_Solution\">Alternate Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternate Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let, for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c1867cd31fa2542f75b0c24655922d93ce901d81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/663b1c8b446e6ce0edc4f65e4560e939b2826d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\ |\\ \\mbox{lcm}(m-1,m-2,\\cdots,m-n+1)\\ |\\ (m-1)(m-2)\\cdots(m-n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"557\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can trivially check that, there is no such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904f27995d33e0d39f43ec959e7cb100516e9396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> works for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/994d4de00361802dd703605742d1cc44fee86565.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> works for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now, consider, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c57d1f5101d7fe31db3c0b42f2d45f5ca0fc81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. By <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bertrand&#39;s_postulate\">Bertrand's postulate</a> there is a prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e185fab10e29b321f44432e2d0dd223d3021477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le \\left\\lfloor\\frac{n}{2}\\right\\rfloor &lt; p &lt; 2\\left\\lfloor\\frac{n}{2}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"166\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>Which implies, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f67c7e39db857fd6862e829346e556804860e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&lt; n \\le 2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>As, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac2b215af2aea25355fd5fe665aeaacf6466394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1 \\ge p,3,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />, there must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and  a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the set, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460d0408027eca63f9475e2cf20a6550d8e30bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{m-1,m-2,\\cdots,m-n+1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff9226e622377da3f58cdeb28c9824a23a80176b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p\\ |\\ \\mbox{lcm}(m-1,m-2,\\cdots,m-n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"299\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7e6071aef1483f06d94437d71f6bcac7cae9b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3p\\ |\\ \\mbox{lcm}(m-1,m-2,\\cdots,m-n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"299\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/857cd7b75619ae25ee7ccafc21babbd774c9f9be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fde5b380793dc7897f3c657edc641a4b5d9873a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> both work for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c57d1f5101d7fe31db3c0b42f2d45f5ca0fc81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>So,\n</p><p>There exists solution for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d8a348130d140aad5a9c23958578539f753241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />,\n</p><p>Only one Solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Q.E.D.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO\" title=\"1981 IMO\">1981 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1981 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173644\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 220/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8344/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.456      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.456      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4006:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173644 and revision id 45769. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}